# kex: check-only
# A method call inside `${...}` is type-checked like any other.
#
# From the type-system audit: interpolation arguments skipped receiver-method
# validation entirely, so a call rejected in direct position was accepted
# inside a string and crashed at runtime — reported at `<stdin>:1:3`, because
# interpolation desugars to a synthesized lambda.
main do
  let n = 5
  IO.printLine("${n.length}")
end
